[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-95942c69-0e5f-4a18-b758-d6c6c933fbf4\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Papers</p><strong>Thu 15 Oct 2026 15:25 - 15:40 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/ase-2026/ase-2026-venue1-forum-16\" class=\"room-link navigate\">Forum 16</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track#program\" class=\"navigate\">Testing and Analysis: Fuzzing and Mutation Testing 3</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/michaelmarcozzi\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Micha\u00EBl Marcozzi</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"95942c69-0e5f-4a18-b758-d6c6c933fbf4\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>Gray-Box Fuzzing in Local Space</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><p>This paper formally defines and tackles a key problem of automated test generation. The coverage problem is specified by a program execution path leading to a certain branching point and an input vector of this execution. The goal is to modify the input vector such that the program running on the modified input follows the same path but the branching point is evaluated to the opposite truth value. Standard fuzzing techniques use bit flips, random fuzzing, and gradient descent to solve this problem. We present an approach that uses numerical methods and linear algebra to transform the problem to so-called local space and applies the mentioned techniques there. An experimental evaluation on the Test-Comp 2025 benchmarks shows some improvements over the standard fuzzing techniques, both for the studied coverage problem and for the problem of test generation for maximal branch coverage.</p>\n<p></p><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1145/3832783.3837510\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"publication-link navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-link\"></span> DOI</a><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/martinjonas\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Martin Jon&aacute;&scaron;\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/martinjonas/f6a92b29-9f59-4040-8820-de4749ddef22/micro-avatar?1793538921000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Martin Jon\u00E1\u0161<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Masaryk University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>Czechia</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/janstrejcek\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Jan Strejcek<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Masaryk University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>Czechia</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2026/marektrtik\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Marek Trt\u00EDk<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Masaryk University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>Czechia</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br></div><div class=\"modal-footer\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2026/ase-2026-research-track/214/Gray-Box-Fuzzing-in-Local-Space\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"btn btn-default navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-new-window\"></span> All Details</a></span><a href=\"#\" data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"btn btn-default\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span> Close</a></div></div></div></div>"},{ "action": "runscript", "value": "$('#modal-95942c69-0e5f-4a18-b758-d6c6c933fbf4').modal({ backdrop: 'static', keyboard: true}, 'show');" },
